note SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
note native/site.om: builder and policy checker for interplane.io and hopbot.org, in seeded Omega.
note Composed after native/lib/sha2.om with a leading om2 line (scripts/build-native.sh).
note   site build OUT HOPOUT     release mode: assemble, check and write both sites; both directories must be new
note   site verify OUT HOPOUT    re-check written output: the exact file set this source builds, every digest,
note                             policy, local links, fragments, and the receipts chain from the output bytes
note   site build --test-data OUT HOPOUT, site verify --test-data OUT HOPOUT
note                             the only mode that accepts made-up data; every page carries a TEST DATA banner
note                             and each output root a TEST-DATA file, which the publisher refuses
note   site contrast             print the button colour arithmetic from public/style.css
note Run from the repository root. Exit 0 pass, 1 refused, 2 usage. A trap (exit 101..114) is also a refusal.
note Inputs: content/routes.txt names every page and file. A page is a front-matter block, a line
note of three dashes, then HTML that is placed in the site layout. Placeholders are {{name}},
note {{#flag}}..{{/flag}} (kept when the flag is set) and {{^flag}}..{{/flag}} (kept when it is not).
note Optional inputs: content/hop.release.txt (the Hop page and the hopbot.org output) and
note content/receipts/ledger.tsv with content/receipts/payload/<sha256>.txt (the receipts page).
note content/hop.copy.txt holds one line, "describes <commit>": the Hop commit the Hop page wording was
note written against. A release build refuses Hop data whose commit is another one.
note content/live.txt holds one line, "map yes" or "map no". Absent or no: the flag map stays unset
note and every link to the forge map is left out.
note Required input: content/papers.snapshot (the papers page, papers.json and papers.bib), written
note by scripts/fetch-papers.sh. Optional: content/papers.sources (source links on Interplane).
note This is a bounded policy checker for reviewed sources. It is not an HTML sanitizer.

